---
source: crates/tempo-mcp/tempomcp/tests/e2e.rs
expression: "e2e::contract(&client).await.unwrap()"
---
{
  "initialize": {
    "capabilities": {
      "prompts": {},
      "resources": {},
      "tools": {}
    },
    "instructions": "Read-only access to a Grafana Tempo instance. Find traces with TraceQL (`search`, with an explicit start/end), then read one with `trace`, which returns a compact span tree with its errors and slowest spans. Use `search_tags`/`search_tag_values` to learn what can be queried. Aggregate rates and latencies are better answered from span-metrics in Prometheus.",
    "protocolVersion": "2025-06-18",
    "serverInfo": {
      "name": "tempomcp",
      "version": "[version]"
    }
  },
  "prompts": [
    {
      "arguments": [
        {
          "description": "Value of `resource.service.name` for the service to investigate.",
          "name": "service",
          "required": true
        }
      ],
      "description": "Find a service's failing requests and group them by the span and error that caused them.",
      "name": "error_traces"
    },
    {
      "arguments": [
        {
          "description": "Value of `resource.service.name` for the service to investigate, e.g.\n`hofvarpnir`.",
          "name": "service",
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "description": "`TraceQL` duration above which a request counts as slow, e.g. `500ms`,\n`2s` (default: `1s`).",
          "name": "threshold",
          "required": false
        }
      ],
      "description": "Find a service's slow requests and identify which span, and which downstream service, the time is spent in.",
      "name": "slow_traces"
    }
  ],
  "rendered_prompts": {
    "error_traces/full": {
      "messages": [
        {
          "content": {
            "text": "Find out what is failing in `<service>`.\n\n1. Call `search` with `{ resource.service.name = \"<service>\" && status = error }` over an explicit recent `start`/`end`.\n2. Call `trace` on up to five of the results and read each one's `errors` list. The first error in tree order is usually the cause; errors on its ancestors are usually propagation.\n3. If the failing span belongs to a different service than `<service>`, say so: the fault is downstream.\n\nReport the distinct error signatures (span name, service, message), how many of the traces you looked at show each, and one trace ID per signature so a human can open it. Do not speculate beyond what the spans say.",
            "type": "text"
          },
          "role": "user"
        }
      ]
    },
    "error_traces/minimal": {
      "messages": [
        {
          "content": {
            "text": "Find out what is failing in `<service>`.\n\n1. Call `search` with `{ resource.service.name = \"<service>\" && status = error }` over an explicit recent `start`/`end`.\n2. Call `trace` on up to five of the results and read each one's `errors` list. The first error in tree order is usually the cause; errors on its ancestors are usually propagation.\n3. If the failing span belongs to a different service than `<service>`, say so: the fault is downstream.\n\nReport the distinct error signatures (span name, service, message), how many of the traces you looked at show each, and one trace ID per signature so a human can open it. Do not speculate beyond what the spans say.",
            "type": "text"
          },
          "role": "user"
        }
      ]
    },
    "slow_traces/full": {
      "messages": [
        {
          "content": {
            "text": "Find out why requests to `<service>` are slow (over <threshold>).\n\nWork in this order:\n1. Call `search_tag_values` for `resource.service.name` and confirm `<service>` is a real value. If it is not, stop and say so — an empty search is indistinguishable from a fast service.\n2. Call `search` with `{ resource.service.name = \"<service>\" && kind = server && duration > <threshold> }` and an explicit `start`/`end` covering the last few hours — without a window Tempo only searches its most recent data.\n3. Pick the two or three slowest traces and call `trace` on each, with `attributes` set to whatever identifies the work (`http.route`, `db.statement`, `url.full` are typical).\n4. In each trace read `slowest`, then walk that span's `parentSpanID` chain in `spans` to see which call path it sits on. Distinguish time spent *in* a span from time spent waiting on its children.\n\nReport: the span (name and service) that dominates the latency, whether it is the same across traces, and the attribute values that distinguish slow requests. Quote real durations. If a trace came back `truncated`, say so.",
            "type": "text"
          },
          "role": "user"
        }
      ]
    },
    "slow_traces/minimal": {
      "messages": [
        {
          "content": {
            "text": "Find out why requests to `<service>` are slow (over 1s).\n\nWork in this order:\n1. Call `search_tag_values` for `resource.service.name` and confirm `<service>` is a real value. If it is not, stop and say so — an empty search is indistinguishable from a fast service.\n2. Call `search` with `{ resource.service.name = \"<service>\" && kind = server && duration > 1s }` and an explicit `start`/`end` covering the last few hours — without a window Tempo only searches its most recent data.\n3. Pick the two or three slowest traces and call `trace` on each, with `attributes` set to whatever identifies the work (`http.route`, `db.statement`, `url.full` are typical).\n4. In each trace read `slowest`, then walk that span's `parentSpanID` chain in `spans` to see which call path it sits on. Distinguish time spent *in* a span from time spent waiting on its children.\n\nReport: the span (name and service) that dominates the latency, whether it is the same across traces, and the attribute values that distinguish slow requests. Quote real durations. If a trace came back `truncated`, say so.",
            "type": "text"
          },
          "role": "user"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "resources": [
    {
      "description": "README for tempo-mcp: TraceQL usage, time windows, the compact trace format, and API caveats.",
      "mimeType": "text/markdown",
      "name": "Tempo MCP operator guide",
      "uri": "doc://tempomcp/guide"
    }
  ],
  "tools": [
    {
      "description": "Run a TraceQL metrics query over a time range (e.g. p95 duration or error rate by route, computed from spans). For standard RED metrics prefer the span-metrics series in Prometheus.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "end": {
            "default": null,
            "description": "Range end: Unix seconds or RFC3339.",
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "q": {
            "description": "`TraceQL` metrics query, e.g.\n`{ resource.service.name = \"hofvarpnir\" } | quantile_over_time(duration, .95) by (span.http.route)`\nor `{ status = error } | rate() by (resource.service.name)`.",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "start": {
            "default": null,
            "description": "Range start: Unix seconds or RFC3339.",
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "step": {
            "default": null,
            "description": "Step between samples as a duration, e.g. `60s` or `5m`. Defaults to\nTempo's choice for the range.",
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "q"
        ],
        "type": "object"
      },
      "name": "metrics_query_range"
    },
    {
      "description": "Search for traces with TraceQL — the starting point for finding slow or failing requests. Returns trace summaries (ID, root service and span, start, duration, matched span count), never spans; follow up with `trace`. Without start/end only recent data is searched.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "end": {
            "default": null,
            "description": "Window end: Unix seconds or RFC3339.",
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "limit": {
            "default": null,
            "description": "Max number of traces to return (default: 20).",
            "format": "uint64",
            "minimum": 0,
            "type": [
              "integer",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "q": {
            "description": "`TraceQL` query selecting the traces to find, e.g.\n`{ resource.service.name = \"hofvarpnir\" && status = error }` or\n`{ span.http.route = \"/api/download\" && duration > 2s }`. `{}` matches\nevery trace.",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "start": {
            "default": null,
            "description": "Window start: Unix seconds or RFC3339. Without `start`/`end`, Tempo only\nsearches recent data still held in its ingesters — pass a window to\nsearch older traces in the backend.",
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "q"
        ],
        "type": "object"
      },
      "name": "search"
    },
    {
      "description": "List the values seen for one TraceQL attribute, e.g. every `resource.service.name` or `span.http.route`. Optionally filtered by a TraceQL query.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "end": {
            "default": null,
            "description": "Optional window end: Unix seconds or RFC3339.",
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "q": {
            "default": null,
            "description": "Optional `TraceQL` query: only list values seen on matching spans, e.g.\n`{ resource.service.name = \"hofvarpnir\" }`.",
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "start": {
            "default": null,
            "description": "Optional window start: Unix seconds or RFC3339.",
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "tag": {
            "description": "Scoped `TraceQL` attribute to list values for, e.g.\n`resource.service.name`, `span.http.route`, or an intrinsic like `name`\nor `status`.",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "tag"
        ],
        "type": "object"
      },
      "name": "search_tag_values"
    },
    {
      "description": "List the attribute names (tags) available for TraceQL, grouped by scope (resource, span, intrinsic, …). Use before writing a query to learn what can be filtered on.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "$defs": {
          "TagScope": {
            "description": "Which attribute scope `search_tags` lists.",
            "enum": [
              "resource",
              "span",
              "intrinsic",
              "event",
              "link",
              "instrumentation"
            ],
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "end": {
            "default": null,
            "description": "Optional window end: Unix seconds or RFC3339.",
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "q": {
            "default": null,
            "description": "Optional `TraceQL` query: only list tags present on matching spans.",
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "scope": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "$ref": "#/$defs/TagScope"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "description": "Restrict to one attribute scope. Omit for all scopes."
          },
          "start": {
            "default": null,
            "description": "Optional window start: Unix seconds or RFC3339.",
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "object"
      },
      "name": "search_tags"
    },
    {
      "description": "Check that Tempo is reachable and ready, and report its version. Fails when the query API itself is unreachable or refuses the credentials.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {},
        "type": "object"
      },
      "name": "status"
    },
    {
      "description": "Fetch one trace by ID as a compact span tree: each span's ID, parent, depth, name, service, kind, start offset and duration in ms, and status, plus the trace's error spans and slowest spans. Pass `attributes` to include specific span/resource attributes, or `raw: true` for the full OTLP document.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "attributes": {
            "default": [],
            "description": "Attribute keys to include on each span, looked up on the span and then\nits resource, e.g. `[\"http.route\", \"http.status_code\", \"db.statement\"]`.\nDefault: none.",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "type": "array"
          },
          "end": {
            "default": null,
            "description": "Optional window end (Unix seconds or RFC3339).",
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "max_spans": {
            "default": null,
            "description": "Max spans to list in the tree (default: 200). The error and slowest-span\nsummaries always cover the whole trace.",
            "format": "uint",
            "minimum": 0,
            "type": [
              "integer",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "raw": {
            "default": false,
            "description": "Return Tempo's full OTLP JSON document instead of the compact tree.\nLarge: every span, attribute and event. Default: false.",
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "start": {
            "default": null,
            "description": "Optional window start (Unix seconds or RFC3339) to narrow the lookup.\nOmit to search all of Tempo's retention.",
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "trace_id": {
            "description": "Trace ID in hex, as returned by `search` (leading zeros may be omitted).",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "trace_id"
        ],
        "type": "object"
      },
      "name": "trace"
    }
  ]
}
